<title>GERMANY: Siemens heads Vienna tram deal group.</title>
<headline>Siemens heads Vienna tram deal group.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Siemens AG said on Tuesday it headed a group which had won a 140 million mark ($93.2 million) contract to build 34 low-floor trams for the Austrian capital Vienna's transport authority.</p>
<p>Siemens said in a statement that trials had been successful and the first tram, designed to be easy for passengers to get on and off, would be delivered in autumn 1997.</p>
<p>The group of companies making the trams is headed by Siemens transport operations in Berlin and Vienna, as well as Austria's Elin Antriebstechnik.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750 ($ = 1.502 German Marks)</p>
